  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Propose and demonstrate an optical floating-gate transistor for neuromorphic computing in which the dielectric 2D photoconductive material (NH4)BiI3 serves as a light-responsive control-gate medium, reducing reliance on an external metal control-gate voltage so that ultrashort low-power light pulses can write many non-volatile resistive synaptic states at ultra-low/femtojoule-scale energy cost, enabling optical training together with efficient electrical inference.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
